core/hailo/meson.build: treat hailo15 as single-arch libdir, like imx8

install_dir is derived from arch_dir, which is only cleared to single-arch (no
Debian-multiarch suffix) for target_platform == 'imx8'; every other
unrecognized platform now hits `error('Unknown target platform: ...')` in this
version of tappas (SRCREV 70c2d5bf2ad31fa47e4c1dc06fd5574055ea8772, pinned at
meta-hailo kirkstone_v5.3.0). hailotools-base.bbclass sets
TARGET_PLATFORM:hailo15 = "hailo15", which matches none of the recognized
values, so meson configure fails outright:

  ERROR: Unknown target platform: hailo15

(At the older kirkstone_v5.0.0 pin this same recipe used, the check was a
single `if target_platform == 'imx8'` with no `else` -- hailo15 silently fell
through to the Debian-multiarch arch_dir instead, which broke the vendor
recipe's own do_install:append() differently; see the 5.0.0-era version of
this patch, superseded by this one.)

Add hailo15 as its own recognized platform, single-arch like imx8. Not folded
into the imx8 branch itself, and not touching the x86/rpi/rockchip/aarch64
branches -- those affect `arch` (used elsewhere for actual cross-compilation
selection), not just arch_dir, and hailo15 should not inherit that behavior.

Upstream: https://github.com/hailo-ai/tappas (SRCREV 70c2d5bf2ad31fa47e4c1dc06fd5574055ea8772)

Signed-off-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -87,6 +87,8 @@
   arch = 'aarch64'
 elif target_platform == 'imx8'
   arch_dir = ''
+elif target_platform == 'hailo15'
+  arch_dir = ''
 else
   error('Unknown target platform: ' + target_platform)
 endif
